there's a very interesting new poll  from the wall street journal about this  upcoming election and it's interesting  not because it says biden is ahead by  nine it's we have many polls that say  that and it may be true  if we uh see the margin of error biden  plus nine might really mean biden plus  two  that's nothing new here what's  interesting about this new poll  is that it breaks down trump versus  biden  along a number of different voting  groups and when you look at it when you  slice and dice the electorate you see  that donald trump is winning among  men barely 47-43 that's interesting  because republicans tend to win among  men by more than four points we'll talk  about that more  on friday trump is winning among white  voters  barely 49 to 47 and donald trump is  winning among people with high school  or less education by a huge margin  nearly 20 points trump is up 54-36  among what are colloquially called the  uneducated now  every other group every single other  group donald trump  is losing some examples include black  voters  biden's up 88 to 80 brutal people with  postgraduate degrees biden is up 65-28  people who are college graduates biden  is up 61-31  among women and among hispanic voters  biden has 57  support and importantly among  independents biden is up 24  49 to 25. now when you see this  you have to consider whether some of  these things are casual  are causal or correlated so for example  the more education you have the more  likely you are to vote  biden we see that right high school or  less biden has 36 support so  36 support if you have some college  biden has 47 support if you graduated  college  biden support goes up to 61 and if you  have a postgraduate degree  biden is up even higher to 67. i believe  this is causal i don't think this is  merely correlation donald trump's  campaign  has been objectively one of lying to  voters  about things he could never possibly do  as president and many people fell  for voting for trump that's the right  terminology not everybody but many  people did  more education makes you less likely to  vote for a candidate  like trump and i would argue for  republicans more broadly so in this case  if you want people  to vote for trump you actually benefit  from hurting education not funding  public schools not dealing with the  student lending crisis  so on and so forth so you really have to  look at this stuff and understand the  link to campaign strategy  and platforms there are ideologically  based positions that  politicians will take or parties will go  in the direction of  but there are also self-preservation  directions  are republicans against education  because some of them see it  as anti-religious indoctrination sure  yeah that exists among  some right-wing voters but a lot of  right-wing voters recognize that the  more educated people are the less likely  they are to vote for them and so that  that's really important to look at  now one last word of caution biden plus  nine  in this poll two and a half months  before the election  is exactly where hillary clinton was  in this poll two and a half months  before  the 2016 election that's all that needs  to be said  trust nothing other than your ability  to vote and to convince others to vote  that's it we are coming up on the david  pakman show's  15th anniversary on august 23rd  on that day we will be sending out to  everybody on our newsletter  a huge membership special the goal being  to have our best month  ever for new memberships this month  because it is our 15th anniversary  to be notified of that special on the  23rd  simply subscribe to my newsletter for  free  at davidpakman.com
 

